+# Upstream Sync Log — PrismML llama.cpp + TurboQuant fusion
+
+Append a new section for every upstream update or port attempt. Do not replace
+historical entries.
+
+This worktree had no ledger until 2026-09-19: the three commits below are the
+first recorded history, reconstructed from the repository and from a fresh audit.
+
+## 2026-09-19: audit — the fusion was not actually complete
+
+Asked whether the fusion was done, and it was not. `c6fbb78` ported the
+TurboQuant types and kernels but none of the integration, so the feature was
+unreachable end to end:
+
+```text
+$ llama-cli -m <model> -ctk turbo3 -ctv turbo3
+error while handling argument "-ctk": Unsupported cache type: turbo3
+allowed values: f32, f16, bf16, q8_0, q4_0, q4_1, iq4_nl, q5_0, q5_1
+
+$ llama-bench -ctk turbo3
+error: invalid parameter for argument: -ctk
+
+$ llama-server --help | grep turbo
+(no output)
+```
+
+Audit findings, measured rather than assumed:
+
+| what | verdict |
+| --- | --- |
+| base build and ternary model | ✅ sound; Bonsai PQ2_0 317.9/45.1 t/s vs 316.9/45.3 on the original PrismML build, i.e. no regression |
+| type registration, block layouts, kernels | ✅ present |
+| integration layer | ❌ absent: `common/arg.cpp`, `set-rows.cu`, `fattn.cu`, `llama-graph.cpp`, `llama-kv-cache.cpp`, `llama-context.cpp`, the CPU path, `llama-bench.cpp` |
+| `ggml_turbo_wht` declaration | ❌ missing from `ggml.h` (defined in `ggml.c` only, so nothing could call it) |
+| `ggml_quantize_chunk` | ❌ no cases, and the switch is `default: assert(false)` |
+| `convert.cu` | ❌ only carried `#include "turbo-quant.cuh"`, no table entries |
+| tests, ledger | ❌ neither existed |
+| file hygiene | ⚠️ 5 files had doubled in length, ~2562 inserted blank lines |
+
+## 2026-09-19: `863eb01` — drop the inserted blank lines
+
+The port emitted every line followed by an empty line, doubling five files
+without changing a statement. The inserted lines had no trailing blank, which
+breaks a naive odd/even split, so the rebuild aligned the non-blank sequences
+against the pristine `9a9394a` version and replayed only the real insertions.
+Checked before writing: the non-blank line sequence is identical before and
+after, so nothing could be lost. Real additions kept in full.
+
+```text
+ggml/src/CMakeLists.txt            632 -> 1265 ->  635
+ggml/src/ggml-cuda/CMakeLists.txt  281 ->  581 ->  303
+ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt   153 ->  323 ->  174
+ggml/src/ggml-cuda/convert.cu      822 -> 1645 ->  825
+ggml/src/ggml-cuda/dequantize.cuh  481 ->  978 ->  498
+```
+
+Verified after: BUILD_OK, `ggml-base.dll` still carries the turbo3/turbo4 type
+names, qwen2.5-1.5B still answers "Paris", Bonsai unchanged.
+
+## 2026-09-19: `7d103ee` — the integration layer
+
+Source of truth was the verified `fusion/turboquant-on-b10964` branch in the
+llama.cpp clone, applied with `patch --fuzz=3` where the base was close enough and
+hand-ported where it was not. PrismML's base is b10615-era, so several things did
+not exist there and had to be adapted:
+
+* the FA vec dispatch has no `FATTN_VEC_CASES_ALL_D(F16, ...)`-style list of bare
+  type names — it uses fully qualified `GGML_TYPE_*`, and the turbo pairs belong in
+  **both** branches of the `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS` switch because the instances
+  are compiled unconditionally.
+* there is no `GGML_CUDA_FA_QUANTS` mechanism at all, only `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS`,
+  so the two CMake hunks that extend the FA_QUANTS default have no counterpart here.
+* there are **7** `build_attn` overloads, not 5, so the WHT-on-q block went in front
+  of all seven rather than the five the older branch patches.
+* `build_attn_mha` has no `ggml_flash_attn_ext_set_n_kv_max` call, so the V-side
+  rotation is anchored after `ggml_flash_attn_ext_set_prec` instead.
+
+Also removed a duplicated FA-instance block that the original port had left behind:
+two `if (GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS)` blocks back to back, the second one omitting the
+turbo instances. It built by luck (CMake dedupes identical sources) but would have
+silently dropped the turbo instances as soon as `FA_ALL_QUANTS` was turned off.
+
+Verification after the port:
+
+```text
+BUILD_OK
+llama-server --help        -> turbo3, turbo4 accepted
+llama-bench -p 256 -n 32 -r 2, qwen2.5-1.5B q8_0:
+    f16 7801.5/174.1   q8_0 7635.8/160.7   turbo3 7449.1/156.5   turbo4 7467.7/151.0
+```
+
+One thing that did not go smoothly and is worth remembering: applying the patch
+with `--fuzz=3` silently mis-placed the `fattn.cu` hunks in the middle of
+`ggml_cuda_get_best_fattn_kernel`, which only surfaced as compile errors. Fuzz on a
+different base is not safe for structural edits; those three hunks were reverted and
+placed by hand.
+
+## 2026-09-19: what the verification turned up
+
+Perplexity on the fusion's own fixture, `-c 512 -fa 1 --chunks 8 -ngl 999`:
+
+| KV | PPL | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| f16 | 10.6801 | correct |
+| q8_0 | 329.4764 | broken |
+| turbo3 | 8038.7921 | broken |
+| turbo4 | 4064.1819 | broken |
+
+The `-fa 0` variants of the quantized types abort in `common_fit_params` (VRAM
+fitting), so `-fa 1` is the only runnable configuration for them.
+
+**This is not the port's fault, and it is not a TurboQuant defect either.**
+Running the same q8_0 KV command against the original PrismML build returns
+329.4764 with byte-identical per-chunk values. q8_0 KV has no TurboQuant code in
+it, so quantized KV is already broken on this base.
+
+**And it is not universal.** SC117 (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B) generates identical text with
+q8_0, turbo3 and turbo4 KV on the promoted b10335 runtime, at the same speed. Its
+head dimension is 256; the fixture is 128.
+
+| model | head dim | quantized KV + FA |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| SC117 (qwen35moe) | 256 | works |
+| ISTA (qwen35) | 256 | works |
+| qwen2.5-1.5B fixture (qwen2) | 128 | broken |
+
+So the accurate statement is **"quantized KV is broken at head_dim 128"**, not
+"turbo KV is broken". This corrects the earlier record on the llama.cpp side, where
+the same measurement was described as a turbo3-specific defect.
+
+## Open items
+
+1. **Bisect quantized KV at D=128 vs D=256.** The fusion's quality fixtures are
+   all head_dim 128, so the gate cannot be evaluated until this is understood.
+   Start with `cpy_ne` / `V_rows_per_thread` in `fattn-vec.cuh`, then the q8_0 path
+   in the same kernel, since q8_0 fails without any TurboQuant code involved.
+2. `mmvq-tq.cu` still not ported (performance only).
+3. The HIP build has `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF`, so `ctest -R test-turbo` has not been
+   run here. The tests are wired into `tests/CMakeLists.txt`; a separate
+   test-enabled build is needed to use them as a gate.
+4. `gguf-py/gguf/constants.py` has no entry for the turbo types.
